Dear [~accountid:5d8368739581710c3032b842], [~accountid:5f3a47cf91e67a003f9a9427], [~accountid:712020:3979a57c-7532-4c17-bd17-1200ae997069],

{panel:bgColor=#deebff}
Thank you once again for submitting your request. After discussing internally with the privacy team, we have come up with the following recommendations:

# For email requests originating from addresses associated with the relevant Bolt account, we can proceed as usual, as these emails are automatically considered verified.
# For requests from unrelated email addresses that are not linked to the Bolt account in question, we kindly ask the requester to submit their inquiry either via an email associated with the relevant Bolt account or directly through the app from the account itself.

This approach ensures a simple and efficient procedure suitable for the current MVP stage of the project.

*We welcome your feedback on whether the privacy team's suggestions are satisfactory or if you have any remaining concerns. We are open to revising our approach based on any feedback or issues raised by customers.*
{panel}

{panel:bgColor=#eae6ff}
Please note that in the future, as the product evolves into a standalone application, we can explore more comprehensive procedures. If this issue proves to be common, we recommend that the CS team collaborate with the PM teams to flag it as a concern that could be addressed with a product solution.

This can include features such as allowing multiple accounts for Bolt Lux products, where some can be designated by executives for their assistants, complete with separate but verified email addresses.
{panel}

