hi [~accountid:712020:0051a059-9c34-4c65-96bf-ddd219dfda7c] thanks for patience while I was aligning the aporach with the team and crafting the response – can you please forward the following response to the User?



{quote}Dear Denis,

Thank you for your data subject request, which was received by us on *30 April 2025* concerning processing of data from smoke detectors where you requested the following information:

# Clarify what specific data was collected in this case and which sensor was used;
# Provide the legal basis for collecting and processing this data;
# Confirm when and how this processing was communicated to you prior or during the use of services.

# *What specific data was collected in this case and which sensor was used*

Our vehicles are equipped with smoke detection sensors solely for the purpose of ensuring compliance with our no-smoking policy, which is clearly stated in our Terms and Conditions available at[ |https://bolt.eu/en-ee/legal/terms-for-bolt-drive/][https://bolt.eu/cs-cz/legal/tnc-bolt-drive/?category=boltDrive|https://bolt.eu/cs-cz/legal/tnc-bolt-drive/?category=boltDrive|smart-link]  (‘Terms’). These sensors are designed to detect the presence of smoke particles inside of the vehicle. In the sensor report we provided to you on *28 April 2025*, you may find the information about the smoke detection sensors and all data collected.



# *Legal basis for collecting and processing smoke detection sensor data*

In accordance with Section 4 of Privacy Notice for Bolt Drive available at [https://bolt.eu/en/privacy/privacy-for-bolt-drive/?category=boltDrive|https://bolt.eu/en/privacy/privacy-for-bolt-drive/?category=boltDrive|smart-link]  (‘Privacy Notice’), we process car sensors data to enable and provide safety features based on Art. 6(1)(f) of the GDPR - processing is necessary for the purposes of the legitimate interests pursued by the controller, which is Bolt. For information on how we process relevant personal data, we refer you to our Privacy Notice, which includes further information about:

* The categories of personal data we process;
* The purposes for which we process personal data;
* The recipients or categories of recipients to whom the personal data has been or will be disclosed;
* The criteria we use to determine how long to retain personal data;
* The sources of personal data received from other parties;
* Your rights in relation to your personal data;
* The existence and envisaged consequences of any automated decision-making/profiling of personal data; and
* Details of any transfer of your personal data to third countries or international organisations and the safeguards used for any such transfers.

# *Confirmation about prior communication of use of smoke detection sensors*

During the sign-up process, all users agree to our Terms, which include a strict no-smoking and/or vaping policy. Additionally, *Section 4* of our Privacy Notice, acknowledged during the sign-up, explains that we process data from car sensors. By accepting the Terms and acknowledging our Privacy Notice, you agreed to adhere to the no-smoking policy and informed of the presence of car-sensors.

*Your rights* 

