* That being said, when providing the requested information, we should still keep in mind the rights of any other individuals whose personal data are contained in the export (e.g., data of Bolt employees, passengers etc.). In other words, we should redact any third-party data unless it is strictly necessary to provide it - this is standard procedure when providing data exports to users, and so should not be too difficult.

{panel:bgColor=#deebff}
*(2) Other considerations*
{panel}

* Even though privacy laws are not directly applicable to the driver’s data, this does not mean that we can definitely share the data freely - Bolt may be subject to other requirements, although admittedly these fall outside of the Privacy Team’s expertise.
