{color:#97a0af}_Tabs: Boolanga financials & Ratio Analysis_{color}

Conclusion below was shared with wider teams in the channel #boolanga-internal-alignment


{color:#0747a6}As discussed in our meeting this week - Our recent financial analysis of Boolanga indicates several areas of concern:{color}

* {color:#0747a6}Liquidity ratios, such as the Current Ratio and Quick Ratio have declined, suggesting a reduced ability to meet short-term obligations.{color}
* {color:#0747a6}There is a higher reliance on debt such as advanced payments from customers.{color}
* {color:#0747a6}Profitability has also significantly weakened, with both the Gross and Operating Profit Margin dropping in 2024.{color}
* {color:#0747a6}Furthermore, Cash Flow from Operating Activities, while positive in 2024 at 50,462, represents a substantial decrease from 627,880 in 2023, and overall cash flow shows a net outflow.{color}

{color:#0747a6}Please note: The above analysis is based solely on numbers so to support our analysis we would also like to request additional financial information below:{color}

* {color:#0747a6}Please provide listings of Accounts Payable (AP), Accounts Receivable (AR), and customer prepayments for 2024 and 2023? To maintain confidentiality, please redact or blur any specific supplier or customer names except Bolt, perhaps by using generic identifiers like 'Supplier A' or 'Customer X'. This will allow us to analyze the concentration of these balances without revealing sensitive business information.								{color}
